{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Validate a broker URL and its TLS material against §8b rules 1–5."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"amqpsEndpoint","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"url","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"caPEM","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clientCertificatePEM","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clientKeyPEM","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AmqpsEndpoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13AmqpsEndpointV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AmqpsEndpoint"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§22.11 rule 3 is why this is a public, tested function rather than a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paragraph."}]},{"type":"text","text":" §8b rule 7 cannot be satisfied by a runtime that never sees a URL"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"— this SDK bundles no AMQP client — so the SDK hands the integrator the check"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead. Documenting the requirement is precisely the failure contract 1.23"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was written to stop: three SDKs asserting "},{"code":"amqps:\/\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a doc comment above a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"call that accepted anything."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What it enforces:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The scheme MUST be ","type":"text"},{"code":"amqps:\/\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every other scheme is refused, ","type":"text"},{"code":"amqp:\/\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"included, and there is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no loopback exception"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (§8b rule 8): this applies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to ","type":"text"},{"code":"localhost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"127.0.0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"::1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exactly as to any other host. §6’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"http:\/\/localhost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dev carve-out does not extend here, and the server has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no plaintext listener for such an exception to reach.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A custom CA bundle is supported, because an in-cluster broker’s certificate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is not issued by a public CA — the common case, and it exists so nobody has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a legitimate reason to want rule 4 relaxed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A client certificate and its key are required TOGETHER. Half a client"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity fails closed rather than connecting without the mutual half."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is no verification-skip option, under any name. It is the most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reliably misused option in TLS: it appears in a dev compose file, it works,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and it travels unchanged into production, where it turns TLS into an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expensive no-op against precisely the attacker TLS exists to stop."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"There is no plaintext fallback. A failed ","type":"text"},{"code":"amqps:\/\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" connection is an error","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to surface, not a condition to work around — and this call offers no way to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"express one.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/amqpsendpoint(_:capem:clientcertificatepem:clientkeypem:)"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/amqpsEndpoint(_:caPEM:clientCertificatePEM:clientKeyPEM:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"amqpsEndpoint(_:caPEM:clientCertificatePEM:clientKeyPEM:)","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Function","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13amqpsEndpoint_5caPEM017clientCertificateF00g3KeyF0AA05AmqpsD0VSS_SSSgA2HtKF","symbolKind":"func","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"amqpsEndpoint"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"caPEM","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?,